  "aiContextParagraph": "Following national elections that resulted in a divided legislature without a clear majority, President Isaac Herzog has initiated the process of establishing a new administration. In a significant development, the President selected opposition figure and former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to lead these efforts rather than the incumbent, Benjamin Netanyahu. This mandate grants Eisenkot 28 days to negotiate with various political factions to secure a coalition capable of governing. Observers are now focused on whether the former army chief can successfully navigate the complexities of the divided political landscape to build a stable cabinet. If these coalition-building attempts fail within the allotted timeframe, the legislative path forward remains uncertain, prompting questions regarding the potential for subsequent political maneuvers by Netanyahu or other opposition leaders. The situation highlights the current parliamentary deadlock within the Israeli political system.",
